.TH tkuopts n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkuopts
.PP
Option checking for tkutils widgets and procs: merge the caller's options over the defaults, and reject an option that does not exist — with the known ones in the message.
.CS
::tkutils::tkuopts::merge MOD defaults argv   ;# -> merged option/value list
.CE
.IP \(bu
\fBMOD\fR — the upper\-case module name (\fBTKUCALC\fR), used in the errorcode.
.IP \(bu
\fBdefaults\fR — option/value pairs, e.g. \fB[array get o]\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBargv\fR — the caller's options.
.PP
Errors:
.TS
l l.
errorcode	message
\fB{TKUTILS <MOD> OPTION <opt>}\fR	\fBunknown option "\-x"\fR / \fBKnown: \-a \-b\fR
\fB{TKUTILS <MOD> OPTION}\fR	\fBmissing value for option "\-x"\fR
.TE
.SS Why
.PP
Up to tkutils 0.44.0 (first build) 24 procs in 20 modules took their options with \fBarray set o $args\fR and swallowed every unknown option — a misspelt \fB\-onresult\fR simply did nothing. \fBtkutlfmt::column\fR had a check, but it ran after the merge, when every given key already existed, so it could never fire (measured 2026\-09\-19). All 24 sites now use:
.CS
array set o {-onresult "" -history 0}
array set o [::tkutils::tkuopts::merge TKUCALC [array get o] $args]
.CE
.PP
Pure Tcl, no Tk. Not in the umbrella: the modules that need it require it themselves.
